# The cockpit's 5 GHz link (DAQ-WIRING.md section 8), the only wireless
# node: lost datagrams are counted, never silent; out of range it is reported
# and comes back; the authoritative log never notices.
# (A datagram counts as lost once it leaves the 32-datagram reorder window,
# about 3 s later; and at 30 % loss three 1 Hz cockpit reports in a row go
# missing now and then: both are checked once the loss has stopped.)
at 3.0  wifi cockpit loss 300
at 8.0  wifi cockpit loss 0
at 11.5 expect cockpit gaps > 3
at 11.5 expect cockpit link == 1

# The cockpit out of range: the Central reports it and keeps logging.
at 12.0 wifi cockpit down
at 16.0 expect cockpit state == LOST
at 16.0 expect COCKPIT_LINK value == 0
at 16.0 expect COCKPIT_BATTERY reason == NO_DATA
at 16.0 expect central event:NODE_LOST >= 1
at 16.0 expect central log_dropped == 0
at 16.0 wifi cockpit up
at 19.0 expect cockpit state == RUN
at 19.0 expect COCKPIT_LINK value == 1
at 19.0 expect central event:NODE_FOUND >= 1

# A low cockpit battery is reported as a value, not a fault.
at 19.0 set COCKPIT_BATTERY 5
at 21.5 expect COCKPIT_BATTERY value <= 6
at 21.5 auto COCKPIT_BATTERY

at 22.0 expect can tx_dropped == 0
at 22.0 expect log intact == 1
end 22.0
